From f1a46a593e09a29e445252378af2806e6a4b7b8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:20:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1007/1286] Take card: spectrum, full-screen views, a wider
 staff printed on Letter

HERESY 1007.
- Spectrum drawer in the take card (heresy-spectrum.js): our Audio Spectral
  Comparator v3 ported to the page with the same method. Mono at 44.1 kHz;
  STFT Hann 2048 hop 2048 with scipy's scaling, floor -80 dB, log or linear
  frequency, the heresy_spectrum palette; Welch average spectrum with the
  SUB..AIR zones; band energy with deltas. Another take can be laid over it.
  The take comes as FLAC; the download is counted and every phase is timed.
  A click on the spectrogram plays the take from there; a playhead follows.
- Full-screen viewer (heresy-zoom.js): Ctrl+wheel zooms around the pointer,
  wheel and drag scroll, + - 0 Esc. Raster pictures are drawn again at every
  zoom; the staff SVG simply comes out larger.
- The staff engraves at 1050 wide instead of 700, and prints on US Letter,
  portrait or landscape, one system per SVG so no page breaks inside one.
- The spectrum's scale buttons have their own class: the kit's score tabs
  handler takes every .stab on the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
